# ============================================================================
#  This repo is served to the public. Treat everything NOT listed here as
#  published the moment it is committed.
# ============================================================================

# The entire blind. This one file is the difference between a blind study and
# a broken one. Never commit it. decode_key.example.json (the template) IS
# tracked, so take care which of the two you are editing.
decode_key.json

# Participant data. IDs are pseudonymous but still subject data, and a public
# repo is the wrong place for them.
*.csv
*.tsv
responses*

# The generated results page. It is built FROM decode_key.json and states in plain
# words which video is the recreation and which is the archive, per pair, so it is
# every bit as sensitive as the key itself. The generator is tracked; its output is not.
report.html
report*.html

# The Sheet decode tab, generated from decode_key.json. Same sensitivity as the key:
# it states in plain words which opaque key is the recreation.
sheet_lookup.tsv

# Video. Binaries in git history are permanent and GitHub Pages has a ~1 GB
# soft cap, so clips are hosted elsewhere and never versioned here.
clips/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mkv

# The static ffmpeg binary, if it gets fetched into the project folder.
bin/

# Credentials of any kind. The one URL that must be public is the Apps Script
# endpoint, which lives in config.js by construction.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Local noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vscode/
.idea/
*.part
